      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office called Preston was established in 1879, and the name changed to Lake Preston in 1882.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Preston%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake Preston was not incorporated until June 22 of 1906, though settlers arrived in the area as early as 1874.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://southdakota.com/cities/lake-preston-sd/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lake Preston is best known outside the area for its first large outdoor swimming pool and its unusual school mascot, The Divers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://southdakota.com/cities/lake-preston-sd/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town site of Lake Preston was platted in 1881 while it was still located in the Dakota Territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
